diff --git a/docs/manifest-schema.md b/docs/manifest-schema.md
index cce4b80..bba1ae4 100644
--- a/docs/manifest-schema.md
+++ b/docs/manifest-schema.md
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-# .wendy artifact format (v1 — frozen)
+# .wendy artifact format (v1 and v2)
 
 A `.wendy` file is a **tar archive** (no outer compression) with a fixed
 member order so the whole artifact installs in one streaming pass from a
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ URL — no temp copy of the payload.
 
 ```
 manifest.json        # FIRST member — everything needed to validate up front
-manifest.sig         # reserved for future signing; absent in v1
+manifest.sig         # reserved for future signing; not verified in v1 or v2
 payload              # the rootfs image, compressed per manifest
 ```
 
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ payload              # the rootfs image, compressed per manifest
 
 ```json
 {
-  "format_version": 1,
+  "format_version": 2,
   "artifact_name": "wendyos-image-jetson-agx-thor-devkit-nvme-wendyos-0.16.0",
   "artifact_version": "0.16.0",
   "compatible_devices": ["jetson-agx-thor"],
@@ -26,14 +26,26 @@ payload              # the rootfs image, compressed per manifest
     "compression": "zstd"
   },
   "bootloader_update": false,
+  "data_encryption": "luks2",
   "min_tool_version": "0.1.0"
 }
 ```
 
+The packer emits v1 with no `data_encryption` field for `--data-encryption plain`,
+so stock v1 updaters can install plain images. `--data-encryption luks2` emits
+v2 with explicit metadata. New receivers retain the live-partition guard for
+both versions; v1 is accepted only on plain data.
+
 Field semantics:
 
 - `compatible_devices` — matched against `/etc/wendyos/device-type`
   (WENDYOS_BOARD_ID). Install refuses (exit 3) on mismatch.
+- `data_encryption` — required in v2: `plain` means an ext4 filesystem on
+  the raw `/data` partition; `luks2` means a LUKS2 header there and ext4 in
+  its unlocked mapper. The installer probes the live raw partition and refuses
+  a mismatch before opening the inactive rootfs slot. v1 artifacts have no
+  field: they remain installable on plain `/data`, but are refused on LUKS2.
+  Old updaters reject v2 rather than silently ignoring this safety field.
 - `payload.sha256` — verified with a rolling hash while streaming the
   decompressed image to the block device; mismatch → exit 3, slot not
   flipped.
@@ -44,3 +56,7 @@ Field semantics:
   new image, not to whoever packaged the artifact.
 - `min_tool_version` — forward-compat gate; older tools refuse artifacts
   they can't handle correctly (exit 3).
+
+`manifest.sig` is still only a reserved member. The payload digests detect
+corruption against the manifest but do not authenticate the manifest itself.
+Artifact authenticity requires a separate trusted signature mechanism.
